  "generation_rule": "Mechanical, tier-based defaults (REQ-120/121; quality of individual rows is a plan-review concern, not a test assertion). Each agent is assigned a tool-footprint tier from its agents/*.md frontmatter: 'author' (no Bash — accessibility-auditor, architect, designer, documenter, integration-specialist) starts at {assertiveness: recommend, autonomy: decide}; 'exec' (declared Bash access) and 'full' (undeclared tools == all tools, including the anticipated pm row) both start at {assertiveness: recommend, autonomy: decide-with-review}. financial-code and schema-migration force assertiveness=gate and cap autonomy at decide-with-review, for every tier and every sensitivity level (REQ-120 acceptance: gated domains always gate). deploy caps autonomy at decide-with-review without forcing assertiveness. sensitivity=sensitive steps autonomy down one ladder rung and floors assertiveness at decide-with-review; sensitivity=confidential forces {assertiveness: gate, autonomy: observe} outright, regardless of tier or domain mode. `fallback` is the exec-tier cube, used by resolveMatrix when a requested agent has no row in any layer.",
